course: dictionary
lesson: 999
title: Boisterous: loud, lively and rough
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Boisterous describes someone or something that is loud, lively and full of energy. Boisterous children are noisy and wild in play, and teachers may ask them to calm down. The word often sounds a bit rough too, so it is not the same as gentle.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like loud, wild, rough and bouncy point to boisterous, while words like quiet, gentle or still point away from it. Try your meaning in the sentence: «boisterous crowd» still makes sense if you think of a loud, lively crowd.
explain: Boisterous can also describe weather or the sea. «A boisterous wind» is rough and stormy, not a child at play. The same idea works in both cases: lots of energy and no calm.
fact: Boisterous means noisy, lively and full of energy, often a bit rough.
fact: «Boisterous» can also describe weather or the sea: «a boisterous wind» is rough and stormy.
fact: «Boisterous play» can be fun, but near roads, pools or stairs it can lead to accidents.
fact: «Boisterous» is an adjective, so it describes a noun: «boisterous children», «a boisterous puppy», «a boisterous crowd».
exercise: What does boisterous mean? | Sad and tired | Calm and quiet | Clean and tidy | *Noisy, lively and full of energy
exercise: «A boisterous wind shook the trees.» What kind of wind is it? | Warm and sunny | Calm and gentle | Silent | *Rough and stormy
exercise: Why might a teacher ask boisterous children to calm down? | It is a rule that children must never laugh | They are reading quietly | *Their loud, wild play could get out of hand or become unsafe | Because boisterous means they are asleep
test: Which word is closest in meaning to boisterous? | Tired | Gentle | Calm | *Rowdy
test: Where is boisterous play most risky? | *Near a busy road, a pool or stairs | At a desk during a quiet lesson | In a library | In a garden with soft grass
exam: Which sentence uses boisterous correctly? | *The boisterous crowd cheered loudly at the football match | The boisterous library was silent all afternoon | The boisterous teacher sat quietly reading a book | The boisterous baby was fast asleep and still
